---
import Layout from '@layouts/default.astro';
import { themeConfig } from '~/theme.config';

const title = 'About This Course for Men';
const description = `What ${themeConfig.name} is: a free, plain course for men leaving porn, gaming, the phone, and alcohol. Christian-rooted and open to anyone.`;
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <h1 class="max-w-[16ch] text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight">A plain course, not a pulpit</h1>
  <div class="lesson-prose mt-6">
    <p>
      This site is a free course for men, written for the United States first. The work is to stop porn, quit the game and the phone when they run the day, leave alcohol if it has a grip, and build a morning you can repeat.
    </p>
    <p>
      The roots are Christian. Scripture shows up in the lessons because it is part of the frame, not because you have to pass a test to read them. If you do not share the faith, take the practical steps and leave the verses. If you do, the verses are there without a sermon wrapped around them.
    </p>
    <p>
      Lessons live in Markdown so they can be added one file at a time. The first open track is <a href="/tracks/break-free-from-porn">break free from porn</a>. A <a href="/tracks/30-day-reset">30-day reset</a> is mapped and marked coming soon.
    </p>
    <p>
      This is not therapy, a church, or a medical service. If you are in immediate danger, call 911. If you are in a mental-health crisis in the US, call or text 988.
    </p>
    <p>
      Brands can <a href="/advertise">advertise</a> at a flat monthly rate. The name of the site is set in one config value so it can change without a hunt through the templates.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
